# Lacuna: About, Testimonials, Contact and Footer recreation prompt

Extend the **Lacuna** landing page (a fictional members' reading room) with four sections that follow the existing hero: **About**, **Testimonials**, **Contact** and a **Footer**. The page is the same single self-contained HTML file (one inline `<style>`, one inline `<script>`, one self-hosted font family) and keeps the hero's look: pure black, Courier Prime typewriter type, paper-white ink, stipple and halftone texture, and the "select a word, strike it out, type the replacement" gesture from the hero headline. Every section has one signature **scroll-driven GSAP animation**: a manifesto that lights up word by word and rewrites itself, a stack of house-rule cards, library cards that slide past on a horizontal track and get stamped, a sheet of paper that rolls out of a typewriter, and a footer revealed from underneath like a curtain, where scattered letters fly together into the giant word LACUNA. Every animation and interaction below must be rebuilt exactly, with the same libraries, timings, easings and numbers.

The hero is built from its own prompt and is not described here, except where this page changes how it behaves (6.2).

