## 6. Motion and interactions (all exact)

### 6.1 Smooth scroll, ready and refresh
Lenis with `{ lerp: 0.165, wheelMultiplier: 1.25 }`, driven by the GSAP ticker (`lenis.raf(time * 1000)`), with `lenis.on("scroll", ScrollTrigger.update)` and `gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(0)`. Lenis is off under reduced motion. The page is ready when `document.fonts.ready` resolves or after 1.5 s; then set `html[data-page-ready]`, build every animation below, and call `ScrollTrigger.refresh()` once fonts and the hands image have loaded and again on `resize` (debounced 150 ms). Everything is created inside one `gsap.matchMedia()` with three contexts: **desktop** `(min-width: 992px)`, **mobile** `(max-width: 991px)` and **reduce** `(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`, so every ScrollTrigger is created and reverted with its media query.

### 6.2 Hero exit and nav behaviour
- **Hero exit** (desktop): a scrubbed ScrollTrigger on the hero (`start: "top top"`, `end: "bottom top"`, `scrub: true`): the copy column goes `y: -12vh` and `opacity: 1 → 0` (opacity finishes at 60 % of the range); the video goes `y: 8vh`, `scale: 1 → 1.06`, `opacity: 1 → .25`.
- **Nav**: it hides when scrolling down and returns when scrolling up: `y: 0 → -100%` over .4 s `power3.out` (ScrollTrigger `onUpdate` with `self.direction`, only after 120 px of scroll). The ticket button's label changes to "SEND IT" while `#contact` is in view (6.11).

### 6.3 Global layers
- **Progress bar**: `scaleX: 0 → 1`, a ScrollTrigger on the whole page (`trigger: document.documentElement`, `start: "top top"`, `end: "bottom bottom"`, `scrub: 0.2`).
- **Film grain**: jitter the tile every 90 ms with `gsap.set(grain, { x: random(-110,110), y: random(-110,110) })` on a `setInterval` (not under reduced motion).
- **Section label**: one ScrollTrigger per section (hero "00 / OPEN", About "01 / ABOUT", Testimonials "02 / READERS", Contact "03 / CONTACT", Footer "04 / INDEX") with `start: "top 55%"`, `end: "bottom 45%"`, `onToggle`: when it becomes active, ScrambleText the label to its new text over 0.6 s (`scrambleText: { text, chars: "01ABCDEF/[]", speed: 0.6 }`).

### 6.4 Block cursor (fine pointer, not reduced motion)
`quickTo` x and y on the block (0.25 s, `power3`), snapping to the pointer on the first move; hidden (opacity 0) until then. While over any `a, button, label, [data-select]` the block turns into a **selection**: it tweens its x, y, width and height to the element's bounding rect (padding .15 rem) over 0.35 s `power3.out`, stops blinking, and its `mix-blend-mode: difference` inverts the text under it, exactly like the selected word in the hero headline. On leave it tweens back to 10 × 18 px at the pointer (0.3 s `power3.out`). Over text inputs the block hides and the native block caret takes over. Over the testimonial cards it stays the small block.

### 6.5 Text reveals
- **Headlines** (Section headline, "TAKE A SEAT.", footer statement): SplitText `type: "chars,words,lines"`, `mask: "lines"`, `linesClass: "line"`, `charsClass: "char"`. Chars from `yPercent: 110, opacity: 0` to 0 / 1, duration 0.9, `expo.out`, stagger 0.018, triggered once at `start: "top 85%"`.
- **Eyebrows** and Labels: ScrambleText from empty to the full string over 0.9 s (`chars: "01ABCDEF/[]—"`, `speed: 0.5`), triggered once at `"top 90%"`.
- **Body text**: SplitText `lines`, `yPercent: 100 → 0`, 0.8 s `expo.out`, stagger 0.07, once at `"top 88%"`.
All of it is skipped under reduced motion.

### 6.6 About: manifesto (pinned, scrubbed)
One ScrollTrigger pins the manifesto: `trigger: .manifesto`, `start: "top top"`, `end: "+=300%"`, `pin: true`, `scrub: 0.5`, `anticipatePin: 1`, driving a timeline of length 10 with these beats:

| t | Beat |
|---|---|
| 0–6.0 | Every word goes `opacity: .14 → 1`, `duration: 0.3`, `ease: "none"`, evenly staggered over the range (each word lights in turn). The `.strike` phrase lights with the others |
| 0–2.0 | The figure's clip-path goes `inset(100% 0 0 0) → inset(0% 0 0 0)`, `power2.out`; the image inside goes `scale: 1.25 → 1` from 0 to 10 (linear) |
| 6.2–6.8 | **Select**: the strike phrase's `--sel` goes `0% → 100%`, `ease: "power2.inOut"`, and its text colour goes to ink (so it reads as a selected block, like "self" in the hero) |
| 6.8–7.2 | **Strike**: `--sel` goes back to `0%` (0.1 s) while the text colour tweens to struck grey, then `--strike` goes `0% → 100%` over 0.35 s `power2.out` |
| 7.2–8.4 | **Replace**: the `.repl` characters go `opacity: 0 → 1`, `ease: "none"`, evenly staggered over the range (they "type in") |
| 0–10 | The 14 loose letters around the figure drift: each `y` from 0 to a random −40…−160 px (linear), plus a tiny rotation drift |
| 8.4–10 | Hold, then the pin releases |

### 6.7 About: house rules (stacking cards)
- Cards are sticky (5.1b). As each next card scrolls over the previous one, the previous one is scrubbed (`trigger: next card`, `start: "top 90%"`, `end: "top 14%"`, `scrub: true`): `scale: 1 → .94`, `opacity: 1 → .45`, `y: 0 → -3vh`, `filter: brightness(1) → brightness(.5)`.
- When a card first enters (`start: "top 75%"`, once): its number ScrambleTexts from "00" to its value over 0.8 s (`chars: "0123456789"`), and its icon draws in with DrawSVG (`drawSVG: "0%" → "100%"`, 1.2 s, `power2.inOut`, paths staggered 0.12 s).

### 6.8 About: stats (odometers)
Once at `start: "top 80%"`: each `.digit` strip tweens `yPercent` from 0 to `-(digit × 10)` over 1.6 s with `expo.out`, staggered 0.08 s from the right-most digit. Then each stat's Label ScrambleTexts in (0.6 s).

### 6.9 Testimonials: horizontal scroll, stamps and card tilt (desktop)
- **Pin and scroll**: `trigger: #readers`, `start: "top top"`, `end: () => "+=" + (track.scrollWidth - innerWidth + 3.8rem in px)`, `pin: true`, `scrub: 1`, `invalidateOnRefresh: true`, `anticipatePin: 1`. It tweens the track `x: 0 → -(track.scrollWidth - innerWidth + padding)`, `ease: "none"`. Keep this tween as `containerAnimation` for the card triggers below.
- **Giant word**: `x: 0 → -30vw` across the same scrub (so it drifts the opposite way to the cards' relative motion, about a third of the speed).
- **Progress**: the counter shows the card nearest the centre ("01 / 06" to "06 / 06"; update with a one-frame ScrambleText), and the fill goes `scaleX: 0 → 1` on the same scrub.
- **Quote typing**: each card's quote is split into chars (SplitText `chars`); chars start at `opacity: 0`; when the card reaches `left 80%` (a ScrollTrigger with `containerAnimation`, `start: "left 80%"`, once) the chars go `opacity: 0 → 1` with `ease: "none"`, `stagger: 0.012`, which types the quote.
- **Tilt**: each card's `rotation` goes from its base value to 0 as it arrives at the middle (`containerAnimation`, `start: "left 85%"`, `end: "center 50%"`, `scrub: true`, `ease: "none"`), then back to its base value as it leaves (`start: "center 50%"`, `end: "right 15%"`, `scrub: true`).
- **Stamp slam**: when a card's centre crosses 55 % of the viewport width (`containerAnimation`, `start: "center 55%"`, once), a timeline on that card runs: the stamp `scale: 2.4 → 1`, `opacity: 0 → .9`, `rotation: base + 18° → base` over 0.22 s `power4.in`; then the card shakes (`x: 5 → -4 → 3 → 0`, three 0.04 s steps, `y: 2 → 0`, yoyo) so it feels struck; and the due-date text gets a brief ink bleed (`text-shadow` from `0 0 6px rgba(17,17,17,.4)` to none over 0.4 s). The stamp stays.
- **≤991 px**: no horizontal track. Each card enters with `y: 60 → 0`, `rotation: base + 4° → base`, `opacity: 0 → 1` over 0.9 s `expo.out` at `"top 85%"`, then the quote types and the stamp slams at `"top 65%"`.

### 6.10 Contact: platen roll-out and typed form
- **Headline**: "TAKE A SEAT." is a **scrubbed** flip rather than the standard reveal: SplitText `chars`, each from `rotationX: -90, y: 40%, opacity: 0, transformOrigin: "50% 100%", transformPerspective: 800` to rest, `stagger: 0.04`, `ease: "none"`, scrubbed from `start: "top 85%"` to `end: "top 35%"` (`scrub: 0.6`).
- **Sheet timeline** (scrubbed, `trigger: .sheet-wrap`, `start: "top 80%"`, `end: "top 15%"`, `scrub: 0.6`, length 10):

| t | Beat |
|---|---|
| 0–5 | The sheet unrolls out of the platen: `clip-path: inset(0 0 100% 0) → inset(0 0 0% 0)` and `yPercent: -35 → 0`, `ease: "none"` |
| 0–10 | Both platen knobs rotate `0 → 540°` (linear) |
| 4–5.5 | The heading types in (counter tween over its characters) |
| 5–9 | Each label types in, one after another (counter tweens, evenly staggered, each ~1 unit long) |
| 5.5–9.5 | Each input's bottom border draws `scaleX: 0 → 1` (origin left), staggered with the labels; the radio chips fade in `opacity: 0 → 1`, `y: 8 → 0` |
| 9–10 | The keycap button fades in with the 3-step flicker (`0 → .4 → 0 → 1`, `steps(3)`) |

- **Keystroke feel**: on every `input` event in the sheet the sheet does a 1 px strike: `gsap.fromTo(sheet, { y: 0 }, { y: 1, duration: 0.06, yoyo: true, repeat: 1, ease: "power1.inOut" })`.
- **Magnetic keycap** (fine pointer): `quickTo` x and y on the button (0.5 s `power3`), pulling it toward the pointer by `0.35 × offset` while within 90 px; on leave it springs back (`x: 0, y: 0`, 0.8 s `elastic.out(1, 0.4)`).
- **Submit**: the form is front-end only. Validate (name and a valid email required; invalid fields get a stamp-coloured border and a 0.3 s horizontal shake of ±6 px). On success the button label changes to "SENDING…" for 600 ms (or until the optional `data-endpoint` request resolves), then:
  1. **Letters fly off**: SplitText `chars` on every label, field value and the heading; each char goes to a random `x: ±(80…320)`, `y: -(120…520)`, `rotation: ±(40…160)`, `opacity: 0` over 1.1 s `power2.in`, `stagger: { amount: 0.5, from: "random" }`. Inputs and chips fade out in the same 0.6 s.
  2. **Confirmation types in** where the form was: "SEAT RESERVED." (Courier Prime 700, 2.2 rem, ink), then a line "We'll write to {email} within a day." (1.1 rem), typed with counter tweens (0.6 s, then 0.9 s).
  3. A "CONFIRMED" stamp (same style and slam as the testimonial stamp, but `stamp` fill at .9 and 9.5 rem across) slams onto the lower-right of the sheet.
  4. The keycap reads "SENT ✓" and is disabled.

### 6.11 Contact: nav hand-off
While `#contact` is in view (`start: "top 60%"`, `end: "bottom 40%"`), the nav ticket button's label ScrambleTexts from "TAKE A SEAT" to "SEND IT" (0.4 s), and back when it leaves.

### 6.12 Footer: curtain reveal, letters assemble, halftone proximity (desktop)
- **Curtain**: pure CSS (5.4). Additionally the footer's inner content is scrubbed (`trigger: main`, `start: "bottom bottom"`, `end: "bottom top"`, `scrub: true`): `yPercent: -22 → 0`, so it rises slightly as it is revealed.
- **Letters assemble** (same trigger and scrub): each `.ch` of the giant wordmark goes **from** a scattered state to rest: `x: random(-30vw, 30vw)`, `y: random(-70vh, -20vh)`, `rotation: random(-70, 70)`, `scale: .4`, `opacity: 0` **to** `x: 0, y: 0, rotation: 0, scale: 1, opacity: 1`, `ease: "power3.out"`, with `stagger: { each: 0.06, from: "random" }`, so the six letters fly together from the middle of the screen and lock into LACUNA exactly as the footer is fully revealed. (It reads as the hero's letter cloud in reverse.)
- **Halftone proximity** (fine pointer, not reduced motion): on every GSAP tick, for each `.ch`, measure the distance `d` from the pointer to the letter's centre; `f = d >= 300 ? 0 : 1 - d / 300`; target `--dot = .9 + (2.6 - .9) × f` (px). If the target changed by at least 0.05, tween the letter's `--dot` with `gsap.quickTo(ch, "--dot", { duration: 0.4, ease: "power2.out", unit: "px" })`; letters near the pointer fill in from fine dots to near-solid, and drift back when it leaves. Re-measure the letter centres on resize and on every scroll event.
- **Marquee**: both copies tween `xPercent: -100`, `repeat: -1`, `ease: "none"`, duration 40 s for one pass. A ScrollTrigger over the footer flips `timeScale` to −1 when scrolling up and +1 when scrolling down (animated over 0.3 s).
- **Placeholder typing**: the reading-list input's placeholder cycles through "Middlemarch…", "Blindness…", "The Dispossessed…", "Pedro Páramo…": each types in char by char (0.07 s/char), holds 1.6 s, deletes (0.04 s/char), then the next, forever (a looping GSAP timeline that sets `input.placeholder`); it pauses when the input is focused or has a value.
- **Back-to-top**: the progress ring draws with DrawSVG from `"0% 0%"` to `"0% 100%"` scrubbed across the whole page (`start: "top top"`, `end: "bottom bottom"`, `scrub: true`); hover: the arrow slides up out of the circle and a copy slides in from below (0.5 s `cubic-bezier(.175,.885,.32,1.275)`); click: `lenis.scrollTo(0, { duration: 2.2 })`.

### 6.13 Mobile and tablet (≤991 px)
No pin on About or Testimonials; no horizontal track; no stacking sticky cards (the three rule cards become a normal column with the standard card entrance: `y: 50 → 0`, `opacity: 0 → 1`, 0.8 s `expo.out`, once at `"top 85%"`); the manifesto still lights word by word but scrubbed over the section's own height (`start: "top 75%"`, `end: "bottom 45%"`, `scrub: true`) with the same select, strike and replace beats at 70 %, 78 % and 86 % of that range; no block cursor, no halftone proximity, no magnetic button; the footer is plain flow and the letters assemble across `start: "top 85%"`, `end: "top 35%"`, `scrub: true` instead.

## 7. Reduced motion

`prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` gives: no Lenis, no pinning, no scrub, no reveals, no stamps slamming, no letters assembling, no odometer rolling, no marquee, no grain jitter, no block cursor, no keystroke strike. Everything shows its **final state**: the manifesto fully lit with "be told what to think" struck out and "change your mind" shown after it, the stats at their final numbers, the three rule cards as a normal column, the testimonial cards in a responsive grid (`repeat(auto-fill, minmax(22rem, 1fr))`, gap 2.5 rem) with their stamps already in place, the sheet fully shown, the footer as plain flow with LACUNA assembled (`--dot` 1.6px). The back-to-top ring is a static 100 % ring. The form still works (validation and the confirmation appear instantly, with no letters flying off).

## 8. Acceptance checklist
- Scrolling out of the hero lifts the headline copy and fades the video; the nav hides while scrolling down and returns on scrolling up; a thin paper bar fills across the top of the page.
- In About, the page pins and the manifesto lights up word by word while the hands image wipes up from the bottom and slowly settles. Then the words "be told what to think" are selected as a block, struck out with a line, and "change your mind" types in after them.
